      "title": "Assistant Curator for Historical Culture and Community",
      "description": "Gilcrease Museum, which houses an interdisciplinary collection representing the diverse heritage of the Americas, seeks an intellectually curious, creative, and self-motivated individual to be Assistant Curator for Historical Culture and Community. This is a new curatorial role, charged with leading exhibitions, acquisitions, research, and interpretation within Gilcrease’s collections of historical American fine art, visual culture, material culture, manuscripts, archives, and rare books. The focus of the Assistant Curator for Historical Culture and Community will be questions of identity, politics, and cultural expression from the past, using rigorous research and dynamic storytelling to convey the relevance of historical objects to contemporary audiences.",
